  "body": "Found while fixing #1594 (PR for issue/1594-tormach-end-g53).\n\n**What:** #1594 removed the `G30` after the final retract in `assets/posts/tormach.cps`: in the user's PathPilot Hub run (770MX sim, stored G30 at machine Z -1.5611) a bare `G30` moved every axis to the stored G30 position (LinuxCNC params 5181-5189), so it drove the tool back down below the part top after `G53 G0 Z0`. Three other bare `G30`s were left alone because the issue scoped only the mill program end:\n\n1. `tormach.cps` `retract()`: `G53 G0 Z0`, `G30`, then `T.. M6` before every tool change. The same low-G30 drop happens there, right before the change (the #1594 comment called this \"worth a follow-up look\"). It is PathPilot's tool-change convention, so this needs the maintainer's call.\n2. `tormach-plasma.cps` `onClose()`: the program ends `G30`, `M30` (no lift first).\n3. `tormach-lathe.cps` `onClose()`: the program ends `G30`, `M30` (X/Z to the operator's preset safe spot; on a lathe \"down\" is not the same risk, but a G30 stored inside the part's envelope is).\n\n**Done means:** each of the three is either kept, with the reason recorded in `docs/decisions/` (e.g. PathPilot requires it and the operator's G30 is documented as a safe spot), or changed with pins and goldens like #1594. Changes to the tool-change G30 wait for the maintainer's decision.\n\nRelated: #1594, #495, #785.\n",
